IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law (8 Del. C. ch. 1), section 212 (voting rights of stockholders; proxies; limitations)
-- and section 214 (cumulative voting). Layer 1, from the text alone. Quote lines are copied from
-- de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt by script.
--
-- Scope for nonstock corporations: s 215(a) says ss 211 to 214 and 216 do not apply to nonstock corporations, except that
-- s 212(c), (d) and (e) do (members for stockholders). s 212(a) and (b) and s 214 are in the section's own words; the
-- applicability rule is in dg4-s215-nonstock-members.l4.

§ `s 212 Voting rights of stockholders; proxies; limitations`

§§ `s 212(a) One vote for each share, and proportions counted in votes`

-- Unless the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise, and subject to s 213, each stockholder is entitled to 1 vote for
-- each share of capital stock held. If the certificate provides for more or less than 1 vote for any share, on any matter,
-- every reference in this chapter to a majority or other proportion of stock, voting stock or shares refers to that
-- proportion of the votes of the stock. So the pieces count votes, not shares (keel F5): this rule is the count.
-- src:778 | (a) Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation and subject to § 213 of this title, each stockholder shall be entitled to 1 vote for each share of capital stock held by such stockholder. If the certificate of incorporation provides for more or less than 1 vote for any share, on any matter, every reference in this chapter to a majority or other proportion of stock, voting stock or shares shall refer to such majority or other proportion of the votes of such stock, voting stock or shares.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(a) (src:778)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation provides for a number of votes other than 1 for the share, on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes the certificate of incorporation gives the share, on the matter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 212(a) the number of votes each share carries on the matter` `the certificate of incorporation provides for a number of votes other than 1 for the share, on the matter` `the number of votes the certificate of incorporation gives the share, on the matter` MEANS
    IF `the certificate of incorporation provides for a number of votes other than 1 for the share, on the matter`
    THEN `the number of votes the certificate of incorporation gives the share, on the matter`
    ELSE 1

-- "Subject to § 213": only a stockholder entitled to vote under s 213 (a stockholder of record on the record date) holds
-- the votes. The number of votes is the shares held times the votes each carries; a proportion of stock is a proportion
-- of these votes.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(a) (src:778)
GIVEN `the stockholder is entitled to vote at the meeting under s 213` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of shares of capital stock held by the stockholder` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes each share carries on the matter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 212(a) the number of votes the stockholder is entitled to cast` `the stockholder is entitled to vote at the meeting under s 213` `the number of shares of capital stock held by the stockholder` `the number of votes each share carries on the matter` MEANS
    IF `the stockholder is entitled to vote at the meeting under s 213`
    THEN `the number of shares of capital stock held by the stockholder` TIMES `the number of votes each share carries on the matter`
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 212(b) Proxies and their three-year limit`

-- Each stockholder entitled to vote at a meeting, or to express consent or dissent to corporate action in writing without a
-- meeting, may authorize another person or persons to act by proxy.
-- src:779 | Each stockholder entitled to vote at a meeting of stockholders or to express consent or dissent to corporate action in writing without a meeting may authorize another person or persons to act for such stockholder by proxy, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(b) (src:779)
GIVEN `the stockholder is entitled to vote at a meeting of stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder is entitled to express consent or dissent to corporate action in writing without a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 212(b) the stockholder may authorize another person or persons to act for the stockholder by proxy` `the stockholder is entitled to vote at a meeting of stockholders` `the stockholder is entitled to express consent or dissent to corporate action in writing without a meeting` MEANS
        `the stockholder is entitled to vote at a meeting of stockholders`
    OR  `the stockholder is entitled to express consent or dissent to corporate action in writing without a meeting`

-- No proxy shall be voted or acted upon after 3 years from its date, unless the proxy provides for a longer period.
-- The last day of the 3 years is the proxy's date plus 3 years (clamped at a month end, keel F2); a proxy that provides for
-- a longer period is not held to the 3 years. Whether the proxy lasts that long by its own terms is a matter of the proxy.
-- src:779 | but no such proxy shall be voted or acted upon after 3 years from its date, unless the proxy provides for a longer period.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(b) (src:779)
GIVEN `the date of the proxy` IS A DATE
      `the proxy provides for a longer period than 3 years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of that longer period, if it has one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the proxy would be voted or acted upon` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 212(b) the three-year limit does not stop the proxy being voted or acted upon` `the date of the proxy` `the proxy provides for a longer period than 3 years` `the last day of that longer period, if it has one` `the day the proxy would be voted or acted upon` MEANS
    IF `the proxy provides for a longer period than 3 years`
    THEN CONSIDER `the last day of that longer period, if it has one`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST lastDay THEN `the day the proxy would be voted or acted upon` AT MOST lastDay
    ELSE `the day the proxy would be voted or acted upon` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in years` 3) `after` `the date of the proxy`)

§§ `s 212(c) Valid means of authorizing a proxy`

-- Without limiting the manner in which a proxy may be authorized under (b), these constitute a valid means: (1) a document
-- executed by the stockholder or the stockholder's authorized officer, director, employee or agent; (2) an electronic
-- transmission to the person who will hold the proxy, or to a proxy solicitation firm, proxy support service organization or
-- like agent duly authorized by that person to receive it, which sets forth or is submitted with information from which it can
-- be determined that the stockholder authorized it; (3) an authorization documented, signed and delivered in accordance with
-- s 116 that sets forth, or is delivered with information enabling the corporation to determine, the stockholder's identity.
-- The list is not exclusive, so a means that is not met is not thereby invalid: the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:780 | (c) Without limiting the manner in which a stockholder may authorize another person or persons to act for such stockholder as proxy pursuant to subsection (b) of this section, the following shall constitute a valid means by which a stockholder may grant such authority:
-- src:781 | (1) A stockholder, or such stockholder’s authorized officer, director, employee or agent, may execute a document authorizing another person or persons to act for such stockholder as proxy.
-- src:782 | (2) A stockholder may authorize another person or persons to act for such stockholder as proxy by transmitting or authorizing the transmission of an electronic transmission to the person who will be the holder of the proxy or to a proxy solicitation firm, proxy support service organization or like agent duly authorized by the person who will be the holder of the proxy to receive such transmission, provided that any such transmission must either set forth or be submitted with information from which it can be determined that the transmission was authorized by the stockholder. If it is determined that such transmissions are valid, the inspectors or, if there are no inspectors, such other persons making that determination shall specify the information upon which they relied.
-- src:783 | (3) The authorization of a person to act as a proxy may be documented, signed and delivered in accordance with § 116 of this title, provided that such authorization shall set forth, or be delivered with information enabling the corporation to determine, the identity of the stockholder granting such authorization.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(c)(1) to (3) (src:780-783)
DECLARE `s 212(c) Way of authorizing a proxy` IS ONE OF
    `a document executed by the stockholder or the stockholder's authorized officer, director, employee or agent`
    `an electronic transmission to the holder of the proxy or to a duly authorized proxy solicitation firm, proxy support service organization or like agent`
    `an authorization documented, signed and delivered in accordance with s 116`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(c)(1) to (3) (src:780-783)
DECLARE `s 212(c) Facts about the authorization` HAS
    `the document was executed by the stockholder or by the stockholder's authorized officer, director, employee or agent`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the electronic transmission was sent to the person who will hold the proxy or to an agent duly authorized by that person to receive it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information from which it can be determined that the stockholder authorized it`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the authorization was documented, signed and delivered in accordance with s 116`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 116 (piece dg1)
    `the authorization sets forth, or is delivered with information enabling the corporation to determine, the identity of the stockholder`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(c)(1) to (3) (src:780-783)
GIVEN way IS A `s 212(c) Way of authorizing a proxy`
      facts IS A `s 212(c) Facts about the authorization`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 212(c) the way of authorizing the proxy is a valid means` way facts MEANS
    IF CONSIDER way
       WHEN `a document executed by the stockholder or the stockholder's authorized officer, director, employee or agent` THEN
           facts's `the document was executed by the stockholder or by the stockholder's authorized officer, director, employee or agent`
       WHEN `an electronic transmission to the holder of the proxy or to a duly authorized proxy solicitation firm, proxy support service organization or like agent` THEN
               facts's `the electronic transmission was sent to the person who will hold the proxy or to an agent duly authorized by that person to receive it`
           AND facts's `the transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information from which it can be determined that the stockholder authorized it`
       WHEN `an authorization documented, signed and delivered in accordance with s 116` THEN
               facts's `the authorization was documented, signed and delivered in accordance with s 116`
           AND facts's `the authorization sets forth, or is delivered with information enabling the corporation to determine, the identity of the stockholder`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (c)(2), last sentence: if it is determined that such transmissions are valid, the inspectors, or if there are none the other
-- persons making the determination, shall specify the information upon which they relied.
-- src:782 | If it is determined that such transmissions are valid, the inspectors or, if there are no inspectors, such other persons making that determination shall specify the information upon which they relied.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(c)(2) (src:782)
GIVEN `it is determined that the transmissions are valid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 212(c)(2) the inspectors or the other persons making the determination must specify the information upon which they relied` `it is determined that the transmissions are valid` MEANS
    `it is determined that the transmissions are valid`

§§ `s 212(d) Reproductions`

-- Any copy, facsimile telecommunication or other reliable reproduction of the document (including an electronic
-- transmission) created under (c) may be used in place of the original for all purposes, provided it is a complete
-- reproduction of the entire original.
-- src:784 | (d) Any copy, facsimile telecommunication or other reliable reproduction of the document (including any electronic transmission) created pursuant to subsection (c) of this section may be substituted or used in lieu of the original document for any and all purposes for which the original document could be used, provided that such copy, facsimile telecommunication or other reproduction shall be a complete reproduction of the entire original document.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(d) (src:784)
GIVEN `it is a copy, facsimile telecommunication or other reliable reproduction of a document created under subsection (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a complete reproduction of the entire original document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 212(d) the reproduction may be substituted or used in lieu of the original for any purpose for which the original could be used` `it is a copy, facsimile telecommunication or other reliable reproduction of a document created under subsection (c)` `it is a complete reproduction of the entire original document` MEANS
        `it is a copy, facsimile telecommunication or other reliable reproduction of a document created under subsection (c)`
    AND `it is a complete reproduction of the entire original document`

§§ `s 212(e) Irrevocable proxies`

-- A duly executed proxy is irrevocable if it states that it is irrevocable and if, and only as long as, it is coupled with
-- an interest sufficient in law to support an irrevocable power. The interest may be in the stock itself or in the
-- corporation generally.
-- src:785 | (e) A duly executed proxy shall be irrevocable if it states that it is irrevocable and if, and only as long as, it is coupled with an interest sufficient in law to support an irrevocable power. A proxy may be made irrevocable regardless of whether the interest with which it is coupled is an interest in the stock itself or an interest in the corporation generally.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(e) (src:785)
DECLARE `s 212(e) Interest coupled with a proxy` IS ONE OF
    `an interest in the stock itself`
    `an interest in the corporation generally`
    `no interest`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(e) (src:785)
GIVEN `the proxy is duly executed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proxy states that it is irrevocable` IS A BOOLEAN
      interest IS A `s 212(e) Interest coupled with a proxy`
      `the interest is sufficient in law to support an irrevocable power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 212(e) the proxy is irrevocable` `the proxy is duly executed` `the proxy states that it is irrevocable` interest `the interest is sufficient in law to support an irrevocable power` MEANS
        `the proxy is duly executed`
    AND `the proxy states that it is irrevocable`
    AND `the interest is sufficient in law to support an irrevocable power`
    AND CONSIDER interest
        WHEN `an interest in the stock itself` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an interest in the corporation generally` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `no interest` THEN FALSE

§ `s 214 Cumulative voting`

-- The certificate of incorporation of any corporation may provide that at all elections of directors, or at elections held
-- under specified circumstances, each holder of stock, or of a class or series, is entitled to as many votes as the votes the
-- holder would otherwise be entitled to cast for the election of directors multiplied by the number of directors to be elected
-- by the holder, and may cast all of them for a single director or distribute them among the directors to be voted for, or any
-- two or more of them. Without such a provision in the certificate, section 214 gives the holder nothing: NOTHING.
-- src:795 | The certificate of incorporation of any corporation may provide that at all elections of directors of the corporation, or at elections held under specified circumstances, each holder of stock or of any class or classes or of a series or series thereof shall be entitled to as many votes as shall equal the number of votes which (except for such provision as to cumulative voting) such holder would be entitled to cast for the election of directors with respect to such holder’s shares of stock multiplied by the number of directors to be elected by such holder, and that such holder may cast all of such votes for a single director or may distribute them among the number to be voted for, or for any 2 or more of them as such holder may see fit.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 214 (src:795)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation provides for cumulative voting at this election` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder's stock is of a class or series the provision covers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes the holder would be entitled to cast for the election of directors with respect to the holder's shares, apart from cumulative voting` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors to be elected by the holder` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 214 the number of votes the holder is entitled to cast in the election of directors` `the certificate of incorporation provides for cumulative voting at this election` `the holder's stock is of a class or series the provision covers` `the votes the holder would be entitled to cast for the election of directors with respect to the holder's shares, apart from cumulative voting` `the number of directors to be elected by the holder` MEANS
    IF `the certificate of incorporation provides for cumulative voting at this election` AND `the holder's stock is of a class or series the provision covers`
    THEN JUST (`the votes the holder would be entitled to cast for the election of directors with respect to the holder's shares, apart from cumulative voting` TIMES `the number of directors to be elected by the holder`)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref 8 Del. C. § 214 (src:795)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation provides for cumulative voting at this election` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder's stock is of a class or series the provision covers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 214 the holder may cast all the votes for a single director or distribute them among the directors to be voted for` `the certificate of incorporation provides for cumulative voting at this election` `the holder's stock is of a class or series the provision covers` MEANS
    IF `the certificate of incorporation provides for cumulative voting at this election` AND `the holder's stock is of a class or series the provision covers`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
